---
/* ============================================================
   Vision 2030 — ink band, centred closing CTA
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   The centred kicker variant, a `d2` headline and the large mint
   button, exactly as the homepage's closing band. Centred with flow
   layout: the export put the button at `left: 485px`, which is what
   centring compiled to at one frame width, not a position.

   The export sets the button label in white. Buttons are the one place
   DESIGN-SYSTEM §6 states the pair outright — mint fill, `ink-deep`
   label — and white on mint is the same 1.2:1 that OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #1
   is about, so `text-kd-ink-deep` it is.

   THIS BAND IS INK AND SO IS THE ONE ABOVE IT. That breaks "never two
   adjacent bands of the same surface" (§2), and it is what the export
   does: HSE and Vision 2030 are two ink bands in a row, so the page
   closes on 192px of unbroken ink between the HSE cards and this
   kicker. Built as drawn; OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #17.
   ============================================================ */
import { about } from "../../data/about";
import Arrow from "../Arrow.astro";
import Kicker from "../Kicker.astro";

const { cta } = about;
---

<section class="bg-kd-ink py-96">
  <div class="max-w-kd mx-auto px-48 flex flex-col items-center text-center">
    <Kicker label={cta.kicker} editKey="about.cta.kicker" variant="centred" />

    <h2
      class="font-display text-d2 text-kd-mist mt-24"
      data-edit="about.cta.headline"
    >
      {cta.headline}
    </h2>

    <a
      href={cta.button.href}
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-8 text-ui-lg bg-kd-mint text-kd-ink-deep px-32 py-16 mt-40"
    >
      <span data-edit="about.cta.button.label">{cta.button.label}</span>
      <Arrow />
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
